The main cost is in the per-field and per-subfield name lookups. The rewrite below keeps the same loop bounds and call order, binds a reference to each field once, and hoists the subfield count out of the inner loop. Since I can't see the `Field` declarations, I haven't changed how names are fetched, so the gain is likely modest.

```cpp
const Field* Mesg::GetField(const std::string& name) const
{
    const FIT_UINT16 count = (FIT_UINT16)fields.size();
    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        const Field& field = fields[i];
        if (field.GetName().compare(name) == 0)
            return &field;

        const FIT_UINT16 subCount = field.GetNumSubFields();
        for (FIT_UINT16 j = 0; j < subCount; j++)
        {
            if ((field.GetName(j).compare(name) == 0) && CanSupportSubField(&field, j))
                return &field;
        }
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```